# Branch consistency (before commit)

On a feature branch, run the full checklist in **`.cursorrules`** → **Before committing** (expanded). Summary:

1. `git diff origin/main HEAD --stat` — skim all behavior changes.
2. **Code ↔ docs** — new/changed `src/emet/simulation/`, `src/emet/app/`, or CLI subcommands → `docs/cli.md`, topic doc, or `docs/simulation_modules.md`.
3. **CLI ↔ docs** — `emet <cmd> --help` matches documented defaults (`resolve_serve_robot()`, dataclass defaults).
4. **Env vars** — new `EMET_*` in changed Python → `docs/environment_variables.md` or topic env doc.
5. **Defaults** — core `emet` CLI, `packages/emet_molmospaces/emet_molmospaces/runner.py`, and `.cursorrules` agree (MolmoSpaces default robot: **stretch**).
6. **Tests** — update CLI help tests when adding subcommands.
7. **Eval / GPU changes** — if touching Habitat runners, overnight scripts, eval harnesses, or `emet eval` / `gpu_preflight`: keep [`docs/cli.md`](../../docs/cli.md) (`emet eval` / `emet jobs` sections), [`src/emet/utils/gpu_preflight.py`](../../src/emet/utils/gpu_preflight.py), [`src/emet/utils/job_registry.py`](../../src/emet/utils/job_registry.py), and overnight scripts aligned; document **`emet eval`** as primary preflight and **`emet jobs`** as required launch for long GPU runs (see `CLAUDE.md`, `.cursor/rules/gpu-eval-workflow.mdc`). Confirm [`docs/experiments/cross_track_smoke.md`](../../docs/experiments/cross_track_smoke.md); run tier 0 + at least one track smoke before claiming merge-ready.
8. Trim AI slop; prefer clear failures over silent fallbacks.
